# A Windows checkout gets CRLF by default, and the files below are read by
# something that does not tolerate it: docker/nginx.conf is copied verbatim into
# the image and parsed by nginx, and /bin/sh runs the Dockerfile's own RUN lines.
# The image builds fine and fails at startup, with an error that names neither
# the file nor the line endings.
#
# CI is unaffected either way -- git stores LF -- so this exists entirely for
# `docker build` run from a Windows working copy.
#
# Matched by PATH, not by extension. This rule used to say `*.template`, and
# renaming docker/nginx.conf.template to docker/nginx.conf dropped the file out
# of it without a word. Anything that ends up in the image now inherits the rule
# from its directory instead of from what it happens to be called.
docker/*    text eol=lf
*.envsh     text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
